  "combinedHtml": "<!-- block: Your manuals | HTML 9290 -->\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n\t<div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12 text-center \"><a href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/sk840_knitting_manual.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/manual_thumb.jpg\"><br><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Knitting Manual</a></div>\r\n\t<div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12 text-center \"><a href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/sk840_operation_manual.pdf\"\" target=\"_blank\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/operation_manual_thumb.jpg\"> <br><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Operation Manual</a></div>\r\n\t<div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12 text-center \"><a href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/silver_reed_electronic_patterns_sk560_sk580_sk830_sk840_sk860_sk890_ec1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/pattern_thumb.jpg\"> <br><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Stitch patterns</a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</div><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n\t<div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12 text-center \">\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/rj1_ribber_carriage.pdf\"> <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/rj1 ribber_manual1.jpg\"><br><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> RJ1 Ribber Manual</a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Printable Reference Cards | HTML 9291 -->\n<style>\r\n    .flex-container {\r\n        display: flex;\r\n        justify-content: space-around;\r\n        width: 80%;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .flex-child:first-child {\r\n        margin-right: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n<div class=\"flex-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"flex-child well_white\">As you learn about the different techniques available with your machine, create your own reference cards to easily remember the carriage settings.\r\n<div class=\"text-center\"><a class=\"btn btn-default\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/technique_card_Silver8401.pdf\" role=\"button\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\r\n Download the cards</a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n    <div class=\"flex-child well_white\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/technique_card_Silver8401.pdf\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/Silver_sk840_card1.jpg\"></a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Terms you must know | HTML 9292 -->\nAt first glance, any knitting machine seems complicated.  Think about the dashboard in a car.  There are lots of dials and buttons and levers, but once you learn the names of things you'll quickly discover what you need to make the car go.<br><br>\r\n<span class=\"yellow_highlight\">Examine the hotspots below and learn the names of the elements that make up your knitting machine.</span>  As you work through this course, these terms will be come second-nature and you will associate the terms with the functions of the machine.<br><br>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Terms you must know | Hotspot 9308 -->\n<aside class=\"legacy-compat-gap\" role=\"note\"><strong>Hotspot not rendered:</strong> “Terms you must know” uses KIN Hotspot plugin data (component 9308). Requires manual conversion or a dedicated hotspot player.</aside>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Tools and Accessories | HTML 9294 -->\nBefore you start to set up your machine, identify the tools and accessories that came with your machine. <br><br>\r\nIf you don't have the tools marked \"essential\" you'll be able to get started knitting, but ask Mr. Google to help you find them. <br>\r\nWhen looking for tools and fun accessories, keep in mind that this is a Singer/Silver/Studio 4.5mm (standard) machine.<br><br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-5 col-sm-offset-1 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <span class=\"yellow_highlight\"></span><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Essential:</b></span>\r\n        <ul class=\"fa-ul\">\r\n            <li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Table Clamps</li>\r\n            <li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Needle Pusher</li>\r\n            <li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Latch Tool</li>\r\n            <li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Transfer Tools</li>\r\n            <li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Claw weights</li>\r\n            <li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Oil (sewing machine oil works great)</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-5 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Consider Locating:</b></span>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>Carriage lock - good for securing the carriage when packing it</li>\r\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.knititnow.com/glossary/249/ravel-cord/term\">Ravel Cord <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> - \"must have\" for certain techniques</li>\r\n            <li>Extra needles - Nice to have on hand - you won't break needles often, but ...</li>\r\n            <li>\r\n                <a href=\"/glossary/283/cast-on-comb/term\">Cast on comb(s) <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a>\r\n\r\n                Some knitters ALWAYS use a cast on comb for even weight across their knitting. <em><small>Silver Reed doesn't supply cast on combs with this machine, but they are available in the marketplace.</small></em>\r\n            </li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <br><br></div>\r\n   <div class=\"text-center\"> <h3><em>NOTE: The <a data-GlossaryId=\"728\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">N-1 Cams (Needle 1) <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> are NOT used with DesignaKnit</em></h3></div>\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Tools and Accessories | Hotspot 9310 -->\n<aside class=\"legacy-compat-gap\" role=\"note\"><strong>Hotspot not rendered:</strong> “Tools and Accessories” uses KIN Hotspot plugin data (component 9310). Requires manual conversion or a dedicated hotspot player.</aside>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Setting up your machine | HTML 9311 -->\nWatch the video below then <a href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/lid_instructions1.jpg\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Download</a> and print out this cheat sheet and tape it to the cover of your machine.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\t<a href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/lid_instructions1.jpg\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" width=\"400\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/lid_instructions1.jpg\"</a>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Setting up your machine | VimeoID 9296 -->\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/798134504\" title=\"Setting up your machine\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Yarn for Your Machine | HTML 9297 -->\n<style>\r\n    .flex-container {\r\n        display: flex;\r\n        justify-content: space-around;\r\n        width: 50%;\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-4 col-sm-offset-1 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <div class=\"flex-container center-block\">\r\n            <div class=\"flex-child well_white\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/98/0.png\"></div>\r\n            <div class=\"flex-child well_white\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/98/1.png\"></div>\r\n            <div class=\"flex-child well_white\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/98/2.png\"></div>\r\n            <div class=\"flex-child well_white\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/98/3.png\"></div>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <br>The 4.5 mm gauge of this machine is perfect for lightweight yarns.\r\n        The only limit is the size of the needles. If the yarn is too thick and doesn't fit in the hooks of the needles, it can split and/or jam the machine.\r\n    </div>\r\n  \r\n        <h3><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Don't Skip This</h3>\r\n        <div class=\"col-sm-4 col-xs-12\">\r\n            <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"Yarn for Knitting Machines\" data-vimeoid=\"527759119\">\r\n                <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1092470097-1c5353bb6555501e8273f58fad80247f1a1625732f095e498ecf755db86f8e54-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n                <div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Yarn for Your Machine | HTML 9298 -->\n<style>\r\n\r\n.yellow_highlight {\r\nbackground: linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 55%, #ffff00 45%, #ffff00);\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<table class=\"table table-responsive  center-block\" style=\"width: 50%; border: 1px solid black\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tbody><tr id=\"YYP0\" class=\"yardrow\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"/images/tools/yarn_standards/0.png\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Lace</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>4000 - 10,000 ypp</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>33-40 sts</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><span class=\"yellow_highlight\">Standard (stranded)<span></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr id=\"YYP1\" class=\"yardrow\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"/images/tools/yarn_standards/1.png\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Super fine</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>3000-4000 ypp</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>27-32 sts</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><span class=\"yellow_highlight\">Standard (stranded)</span></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr id=\"YYP2\" class=\"yardrow\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"/images/tools/yarn_standards/2.png\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Fine</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>2000-3000</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>23-26</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><span class=\"yellow_highlight\"> Standard / Double Bed</span></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr id=\"YYP3\" class=\"yardrow\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"/images/tools/yarn_standards/3.png\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Light</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>1000-2000</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>21-24</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Mid-Gauge/<span class=\"yellow_highlight\">Standard</span></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr id=\"YYP4\" class=\"yardrow\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"/images/tools/yarn_standards/4.png\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Medium</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>800-1000</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>16-20</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Mid-Gauge/Bulky</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr id=\"YYP5\" class=\"yardrow\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"/images/tools/yarn_standards/5.png\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Bulky</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>500-800</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>12-15</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Bulky</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr id=\"YYP6\" class=\"yardrow\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td><img src=\"/images/tools/yarn_standards/6.png\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>Super Bulky</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>100-500</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>6-11</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td>May not be appropriate.</td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr></tbody></table>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Plain Knitting | HTML 9302 -->\n<span class=\"handwriting\">Understanding how to set your carriage for <b>PLAIN KNITTING</b> is essential</span><br><br>\r\nIt is a good habit to always check your carriage settings before starting a new technique or a new piece of knitting.  It's easy to have your carriage set for patterning, then come back days later and be surprised that the machine isn't knitting as expected.<br><br>\r\n<b>\r\nEvery time you sit down to knit, take time to double check the settings.</b>\r\n\r\n<br><br><br>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Plain Knitting | HTML 9303 -->\n<div class=\" center-block\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col-sm-4 col-xs-12\">\r\n\t\t\t<div class=\"table-responsive\">\r\n    <table class=\"table table-bordered\">\r\n       \r\n        <tbody>\r\n            <tr>\r\n                <td><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i> 1. Cam Lever</td>\r\n                <td><center><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/plain_setting.jpg\" width=\"25\"></center></td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n          <tr>\r\n                <td><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i> 2. Stitch Dial</td>\r\n                <td><center>5</center></td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n             <tr>\r\n                <td><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i> 3.  Russel Lever(s)</td>\r\n                   <td><center><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/russel_lever.jpg\"></center></td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n\r\n                <td><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i> 4. Weaving Knob(s)</td>\r\n                <td><center><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/weaving _knob.jpg\"> (up)</center></td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n                <td><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i> 5. Yarn Feeder</td>\r\n                <td><center><img src=\"/images/machines/details/360_Icon7.png\"></center></td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n</div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t<div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n\t\t\t\t<img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/plain_knitting.jpg\">\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n</div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: The Proper Way to Knit | HTML 9304 -->\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/86/lightbulb_icon_40x40.png\"> <span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:1.5em\">Save your back, neck and shoulders</span><br><br>\r\nIn the videos in this course, you'll see me pushing the carriage with one hand.   BAD!!!!  I'm reaching around the camera.<br><br>\r\nWhen you are knitting <b>use both hands</b> and push and pull alternately to move the carriage.<br><br>\r\nMany knitters also adjust their knitting table so they can stand while knitting.  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><div class='embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9'><iframe src='https://player.vimeo.com/video/530014000' frameborder='0' webkitAllowFullScreen mozallowfullscreen allowFullScreen></iframe></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: The Proper Way to Knit | HTML 9305 -->\n<img class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"250\" src=\"/path/images/1558/woman_silhouette1.gif\">\r\n\t\t<h3> Arm, hand and wrist position</h3>\r\n\t\t<b>STOP! LOOK AT THE POSITION OF YOUR\r\n\t\t\tHAND AND WRIST IN RELATION TO YOUR\r\n\t\t\tELBOW.</b>Many knitters will find their elbow is\r\n\t\tbelow the level of the wrist and hand. <br><br><b>Knitting\r\n\t\t\tin this position, after a time, will create an ache\r\n\t\t\tand pain through the neck and across the\r\n\t\t\tshoulders.</b>\r\n\t\t\tTry sitting higher so that your elbow\r\n\t\tis <b>slightly above</b> the wrist and hand.\r\n\t\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: The Proper Way to Knit | HTML 9306 -->\n<h3>More tips</h3>\r\n\t<ul class=\"fa-ul\">\r\n\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>A stool for your feet may be needed or your machine table or stand may have to be lowered. </li><br>\r\n\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> If you\r\n\t\t\thave a stand to use your machine,\r\n\t\t\tthe same elbow position is needed. <em>(elbows slightly above the hands)</em></li><br>\r\n\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Try standing to knit. Use an adjustable table to keep the elbow position correct.\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<a data-popupcontentid=\"10005\" class=\"pathpopup\"><i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Here's what I use<br></a>\r\n\t\t</li><br>\r\n\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>\r\n\t\t\t<a href=\"#light\" data-toggle=\"collapse\"><b><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Good lighting is a must</b></a>\r\n\t\t\t<div id=\"light\" class=\"collapse hidden-print\">\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"subvideopopup\" data-videotitle=\"Knitting Machine Lighting Fixture\" data-vimeoid=\"151858745\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/551702337-37ad84787c7c2b538e8e57a7297fe7a73c9ccec35eab752146eece8a322b0b56-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t</li><br>\r\n\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>A clean (and oiled) machine bed and carriage are essential.</li>\r\n\t\t<br>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Electronics Set up for DAK | HTML 9320 -->\n<style>\r\n    .circle {\r\n        width: 25px;\r\n        height: 25px;\r\n        border-radius: 50%;\r\n        box-sizing: border-box;\r\n        text-align: center;\r\n        display: inline-block;\r\n        line-height: 25px;\r\n        background-color: #9E2065;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .circle a {\r\n        text-decoration: none;\r\n        color: #fff;\r\n        font-size: 16px;\r\n    }\r\nhr.style13 {\r\nheight: 10px;\r\nborder: 0;\r\nbox-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\">This machines uses external devices for automatic patterning. (Unlike Brother/Knit-King machines with built-in electronics) <br><br>\r\n        This course focuses on how to use DesignaKnit to talk to the machine and choose the right needles for stitch patterns. <br>\r\n\r\n        <h3>REQUIRED:</h3>\r\n        <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">1</a></div> PC and DesignaKnit\r\n        <br><br>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">2</a></div> SilverLink 4 or 5 box\r\n        <br><br>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">3</a></div> USB cable (from PC to SilverLink Box)\r\n        <br><br>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">4</a></div> Curl Cord (from SilverLink Box to Carriage)\r\n        <br><br>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">5</a></div> Power cord for SilverLink Box\r\n<br><br><h3><em>NOTE: The <a data-GlossaryId=\"728\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">N-1 Cam (Needle 1) <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> is NOT used with DesignaKnit</em></h3>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/cables2.jpg\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Electronics Set up for DAK | HTML 9323 -->\n<style>\r\nimg.ctr{\r\ndisplay: block;\r\nmargin-left: auto;\r\nmargin-right: auto; }\r\n/* styling paper */\r\n#paper {\r\nwidth: 400px;\r\nheight: 500px;\r\nposition: relative;\r\nmargin: 20px auto;\r\npadding-top: 40px;\r\npadding-bottom: 40px;\r\nbackground-color: white;\r\nbox-shadow: 0px 0px 5px 0px #888;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* styling red vertical line */\r\n#paper::before {\r\ncontent: '';\r\nwidth: 2px;\r\nheight: 100%;\r\nposition: absolute;\r\ntop: 0;\r\nleft: 40px;\r\nbackground-color: rgba(158,32,101,0.6);\r\n\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* styling blue horizontal lines */\r\n#pattern {\r\nheight: 100%;\r\nbackground-image: repeating-linear-gradient(white 0px, white 24px, teal 25px);\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* styling text content */\r\n#content {\r\npadding-top: 6px;\r\npadding-left: 56px;\r\npadding-right: 16px;\r\nline-height: 25px;\r\nfont-size: 16px;\r\nletter-spacing: 1px;\r\nword-spacing: 5px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/silver_knit_connect.jpg\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\">\r\n<div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-12 col-md-5\">\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-responsive ctr\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/silverlink.jpg\">\r\n<div id=\"paper\">\r\n<div id=\"pattern\">\r\n<div id=\"content\">\r\n<br><br>\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"color: #9E2065\"></i> Connect the PC  <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">1</a></div> to the SilverLink Box <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">2</a></div> with the USB Cable <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">3</a></div><br><br>\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"color: #9E2065\"></i> Connect power to the SilverLink Box with the power cord <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">5</a></div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"color: #9E2065\"></i> Position the Curl Cord on the tension mast (cable toward you)<div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">6</a></div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"color: #9E2065\"></i> Connect the Curl Cord to the carriage<div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">5</a></div>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Needles | HTML 9645 -->\n\t<img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/840_needles1.jpg\"<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a href=\"/store/product/827/replacement-needles-silver-reed-lot-of/itemdetails\" target=\"_blank\"><i class=\"fa fa-shopping-cart fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Buy replacement  MAIN BED needles from Knit it Now</a><br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a href=\"/store/product/828/replacement-needles-silver-reed-ribber-lot-of/itemdetails\" target=\"_blank\"><i class=\"fa fa-shopping-cart fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Buy replacement RIBBER needles from Knit it Now</a><br><br>\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"https://www.knititnow.com/knititnow/store/thumbnails/10needles4.jpg\"></a></div>\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Replace a Needle | HTML 9466 -->\n<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\"> Don't try to bend (or \"repair) a bent needle .. replace it!</span><br><br>\r\n\r\nHeaven forbid that you bend a needle (it happens). <br><br>\r\nReplacing it shouldn't be a problem.  Keep spare needles on hand.<br><br>\r\nIf you don't have a spare needle, you can \"borrow\" a needle from the end of the needlbed tempororarily<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Replace a Needle | VimeoID 9465 -->\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/569614718\" title=\"Replace a Needle\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Insert Point Cams | VimeoID 9505 -->\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/825599756\" title=\"Insert Point Cams\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>"
